## 2. Advanced S3 Features

To architect cost-effective, performant, and resilient applications, you must master advanced S3 features[cite: 1].

### S3 Storage Classes & Lifecycle Management
Optimizing storage tiering directly influences cost-efficiency[cite: 1].

| Storage Class | Designed Availability | Minimum Storage Duration | Retrieval Fees | Ideal Use Case |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **S3 Standard** | 99.99% | None | None | Active, frequently accessed data. |
| **S3 Standard-IA** | 99.9% | 30 days | Per GB retrieved | Infrequently accessed data needed immediately when requested. |
| **S3 One Zone-IA** | 99.5% | 30 days | Per GB retrieved | Non-critical, reproducible data stored in a single AZ (lower cost). |
| **S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval** | 99.9% | 90 days | Per GB retrieved | Archival data requiring millisecond retrieval times. |
| **S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval** | 99.99% | 90 days | Per GB retrieved | Archive data with retrieval options from 1–5 mins (Expedited), 3–5 hrs (Standard), or 5–12 hrs (Bulk). |
| **S3 Glacier Deep Archive** | 99.9% | 180 days | Per GB retrieved | Long-term digital preservation with 12-hour (Standard) or 48-hour (Bulk) retrievals. |
| **S3 Intelligent-Tiering** | 99.9% | None | None | Data with unknown or changing access patterns. Automates tiering across Frequent, Infrequent, Archive Instant, Archive, and Deep Archive access tiers without operational overhead. |

* **S3 Lifecycle Rules:** Used to automate transitions between classes (`Transition actions`) or permanent deletion (`Expiration actions`)[cite: 1].
  * Can target current object versions or noncurrent object versions[cite: 1].
  * Useful for compliance or optimizing logs[cite: 1].

### S3 Versioning & Object Locks
* **Versioning:** Keeps multiple variants of an object in the same bucket[cite: 1].
  * Enabled at the bucket level[cite: 1]. Once enabled, it can only be **Suspended**, not completely disabled[cite: 1].
  * Deleting an object with versioning enabled creates a **Delete Marker**[cite: 1]. To permanently delete an object, you must specify the exact `Version ID`[cite: 1].
* **S3 Object Lock:** Adheres to the **WORM (Write Once, Read Many)** model[cite: 1]. Requires versioning to be enabled first[cite: 1].
  * **Retention Period:** Blocks deletion for a specified time[cite: 1].
    * *Compliance Mode:* The retention period cannot be shortened, and the protection cannot be bypassed by any user (including the root account)[cite: 1].
    * *Governance Mode:* Special permissions (`s3:BypassGovernanceRetention`) allow authorized roles to bypass or alter settings[cite: 1].
  * **Legal Hold:** Places an indefinite hold on an object until explicitly removed[cite: 1]. No retention dates apply[cite: 1].

### Replication (CRR and SRR)
Replication requires **Versioning** enabled on both the Source and Destination buckets[cite: 1].
* **Cross-Region Replication (CRR):** Replicates objects across buckets in different AWS Regions[cite: 1]. Used for geo-redundancy, lower latency requirements, or compliance[cite: 1].
* **Same-Region Replication (SRR):** Replicates objects across buckets in the same Region[cite: 1]. Used for log aggregation, or isolating production and test environments[cite: 1].
* *Note:* S3 can replicate objects across different AWS accounts[cite: 1]. Existing objects are *not* automatically replicated by default when replication rules are first turned on (requires S3 Batch Operations)[cite: 1].

### S3 Performance Optimization
* **Multipart Upload:** Breaks files into smaller chunks[cite: 1]. Uploads occur in parallel, maximizing throughput and enabling recovery from network errors mid-upload[cite: 1].
* **S3 Transfer Acceleration:** Leverages AWS Edge Locations[cite: 1]. Traffic traverses Amazon's optimized global backbone network instead of the public internet to reach the target bucket[cite: 1].
* **S3 Select & Amazon Athena:** 
  * **S3 Select:** Filters data using simple SQL expressions at the storage layer, returning only a subset of data (e.g., rows/columns from a CSV or JSON file), saving network transfer and computing overhead[cite: 1].
  * **Amazon Athena:** A serverless query service used to analyze large volumes of unstructured/structured data directly in S3 via standard SQL[cite: 1].

